# Trivy vulnerability exceptions — SCOPED, DATED, AND JUSTIFIED
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ BEFORE ADDING ANYTHING HERE
#
# This file suppresses SPECIFIC CVE IDs. It does not lower the severity
# threshold and does not disable the scan. Every other HIGH/CRITICAL finding
# still fails the build before the image reaches ECR.
#
# Adding an entry is a RISK ACCEPTANCE DECISION, not a build fix. Each one
# must carry: why the fix is unavailable, the exploit path, why it does not
# apply to this application, and an expiry date.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ACCEPTED ON 2026-09-05 — REVIEW BY 2026-10-05
#
# Component : org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core 10.1.55
#             (transitive, via spring-boot-starter-web on Spring Boot 3.5.16)
# Fixed in  : Tomcat 10.1.58
#
# WHY NOT SIMPLY UPGRADE:
# No released Spring Boot version ships Tomcat 10.1.58. Boot 3.5.16 is the
# newest stable release (verified against upstream release tags) and manages
# 10.1.55. This is an upstream release-timing gap. The project already moved
# 3.4.1 -> 3.5.16 specifically to close the earlier Tomcat advisories, which
# it did; these three were disclosed against the newer version.
#
# WHY THE EXPOSURE IS LIMITED HERE:
# All three are bypasses of Tomcat's OWN authentication and security-constraint
# machinery. This application:
#   * defines no <security-constraint> and no protected resources
#   * uses no DIGEST authentication
#   * uses no FORM authentication
#   * has no Spring Security dependency
#   * serves only public endpoints: /, /api/info, /actuator/health,
#     /actuator/readiness, /actuator/prometheus
# There is no authentication layer present for an attacker to bypass.
#
# THIS ACCEPTANCE BECOMES INVALID IMMEDIATELY IF ANY OF THESE HAPPEN:
#   * Spring Security or any authentication mechanism is added
#   * any endpoint becomes access-controlled
#   * a security-constraint, DIGEST or FORM login config is introduced
#   * management endpoints beyond health/prometheus are exposed
# In any of those cases, remove these entries and upgrade Tomcat first.
#
# HOW TO RETIRE THIS FILE (preferred outcome):
#   1. Watch for a Spring Boot release managing Tomcat >= 10.1.58 and bump the
#      parent version in pom.xml. Verify the release exists before committing.
#   2. Or set <tomcat.version>10.1.58</tomcat.version> in pom.xml once that
#      release is on Maven Central, and delete these entries.
#   3. Enable GitHub Dependabot (free on public repositories) so these bumps
#      are proposed automatically instead of discovered by a failed deploy.

# Security constraint bypass due to improper access control.
# Exploit path: crafted request bypasses a <security-constraint> mapping.
# Not applicable: no security constraints are defined in this application.
CVE-2026-65182

# Authentication bypass via limited replay attack in the DIGEST authenticator.
# Exploit path: replay of a captured DIGEST auth exchange.
# Not applicable: DIGEST authentication is not configured or used.
CVE-2026-65905

# Unauthorized resource access via FORM authentication bypass.
# Exploit path: crafted request against the FORM login flow.
# Not applicable: FORM authentication is not configured or used.
CVE-2026-68525
